      "text": "Panama City and the Panama Canal"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "cb75b548e7b2bb929caec834769b102d10770f376f49d1e7cdbb57069616140d",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-wm-p7lxhnqwgwc",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "The tour lasts around six hours. One of your first stops is the Miraflores Locks, where you can watch the canal in operation as ships pass through. The IMAX cinema shows a 45-minute film about the construction and operation of the Panama Canal. It is in English with Spanish subtitles and narrated by Morgan Freeman.\n\nYou'll then see the capital's historic and modern districts, drive through the residential part of the former Canal Zone where Americans who built and operated the canal once lived, and visit Balboa Avenue along Panama Bay.\n\nCasco Antiguo retains the narrow streets, squares and parks of the city's historic quarter. The route takes you through Plaza de Francia and to San José Church, where you'll learn the story of its golden altar. Another stop is the Amador Causeway, which links what were once three separate islands: Naos, Perico and Flamenco.\n\nAfter the tour, transfer back to your hotel. Overnight in Panama City."
    },
